repository-code: "https://github.com/papers-data/achievement-ratings-divergence-replication"
abstract: >-
  Semester-level data behind an eleven-year longitudinal case study of one
  introductory programming course at the Tuluá campus of Universidad del Valle:
  the eighteen-semester official grade-outcome series (2015-II to 2026-I), the
  fourteen-semester institutional course-evaluation series (2018-I to 2026-I),
  the codebook and two independent per-comment codings for the Longitudinal
  Directed Content Analysis of open-ended evaluation comments, the segmented
  interrupted-time-series script, and the analysis reports behind the article's
  tables. No student-level record is released. The grade series is aggregated to
  the semester, and evaluation comments carry opaque identifiers with no
  verbatim text.
keywords:
  - computing education
  - introductory programming
  - CS1
  - flipped classroom
  - course evaluation
  - longitudinal study
  - interrupted time series
